    "label": {
      "en": "B - couples"
    },
    "short_label": {
      "en": "$chall_B2"
    },
    "description": {
      "en": "Income threshold B used in the child-related budget's taper formula 'C − D × max(0, income − B)', applied when the recipient tax unit is a couple with a fiscal partner, where 'income' is the combined taxable income of both partners in Box 1 and Box 3. It is consumed in chall_nl/BenCalc's comp_perTU parameter (alongside $chall_B1) when computing the income/age-related child allowance entitlement. Per the Country Report, since 2020 this couples' threshold has been set above the single-parent threshold; the table shows it fluctuating from €39,596 (2022) up to €43,397 (2023) then down to €35,849 (2024) and €37,545 (2025), with the model's latest value at €39,141/year."
    },
    "explanation": {
      "en": "EUROMOD function group: CT - table 2.18"
    },
